{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q418179","formula":"C₂₂H₁₉ClO₃","hill":"C22H19ClO3","elements":["H","C","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":22.0,"H":19.0,"O":3.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Atovaquone","ru":"Атовакуон","uk":"Атоваквон"},"descriptions":{"en":"Atovaquone, sold under the brand name Mepron, is an naphthoquinone antiprotozoal medication used in the prevention and treatment Pneumocystis jirovecii pneumonia (PCP), and malaria (in combination with proguanil), as well as for treatment of babesiosis (in combination with azithromycin). Atovaquone is an analogue of ubiquinone (coenzyme Q10) and exerts its pharmaceutical effects by binding to the ubiquinone binding site on the parasitic mitochondrial cytochrome bc1 complex, thus inhibiting a step of protozoal pyrimidine synthesis. Atovaquone is a hydroxy-1,4-naphthoquinone, an analog of both ubiquinone and lawsone.","ru":"Атовакуон — химическое соединение, относящееся к классу нафтохинонов. Представляет собой гидрокси-1,4-нафтохинон, аналог убихинона, с антипневмоцистной активностью. В США изготавливается в жидкой форме, как пероральная суспензия, под торговым названием Мерпон.","uk":"Атовакво́н — синтетичний антипротозойний препарат, що є похідним гідроксинафтохінону, для прийому всередину."},"fame":26,"pubchemCid":74989,"mass":366.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CC(CCC1C2=CC=C(C=C2)Cl)C3=C(C4=CC=CC=C4C(=O)C3=O)O","inchikey":"BSJMWHQBCZFXBR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-[4-(4-chlorophenyl)cyclohexyl]-4-hydroxynaphthalene-1,2-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"74989","atoms":45,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":8.639,"y":-0.444,"z":0.049,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-2.376,"y":-2.527,"z":0.178,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.167,"y":2.087,"z":-0.209,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.718,"y":2.763,"z":-0.215,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.157,"y":-0.518,"z":0.033,"el":"C"},